      "src": "images/cartridges/22-hornet/hero.webp",
      "alt": "A single .22 Hornet cartridge lying on orange millimetre graph paper. The brass case is long, slim and noticeably tapered, ending in a short shoulder and a narrow neck, and carries a copper-jacketed bullet with an exposed grey lead tip. A thin rim projects at the base.",
      "caption": "A .22 Hornet loaded with a soft-point bullet, on 1 mm graph paper. The taper down the case body and the small, shallow shoulder are inherited from the black-powder .22 WCF the round was developed out of; the projecting rim is what a break-action or single-shot rifle extracts on.",
