      "src": "images/cartridges/22-hornet/comparison.webp",
      "alt": "Four small brass cartridges standing on a sand-coloured surface, rising in height from left to right. The two on the left are short and plain-walled with a flat rim; the third is longer with a lead-tipped jacketed bullet; the tallest on the right is a bottlenecked case with a red-tipped copper bullet.",
      "caption": "From the left, .22 Short, .22 Long Rifle, .22 Winchester Magnum Rimfire and .22 Hornet with a 35-grain polymer-tipped bullet. The first three are rimfire; the Hornet is the centrefire round in the same bullet diameter, and roughly twice the case length of the .22 WMR.",
